## EURYTHMICS - SWEET DREAMS (ARE MADE OF THIS)
#  Full Arrangement Cover for PULP / SKRED. 125 BPM, C minor, 96 bars (~3:04).
#  Written & Produced by Annie Lennox & Dave Stewart (1983).
#  Self-contained: drums from built-in waves 82-99, inline K-synth riser.
#  Uses n>d to convert note name strings to MIDI note streams.
#  Load:   [sweet_dreams_full.sk] /ls
#  Start:  play        Stop:  stop
#
#  VOICE MAP (all labeled via [name] vt):
#    v0  four-on-the-floor kick (w82) + v5 sub punch (w0)
#    v1  gated 80s snare (w83) + v4 electronic clap (w86)
#    v2  closed hat 16ths (w84)  v3  open hat offbeat (w85)
#    v6  main bass riff saw centre (w15) + v7 partner square (w16, right)
#    v8  Annie Lennox vocal lead centre (w15) + v9 (left w15), v10 (right w16)
#    v11 analog synth solo centre (w15) + v12 partner (w16)
#    v13 counter-riff plucky square left (w16)
#    v16 K-synth build riser (w301)
#    v17 crash cymbal (w94)
#    v18 hi tom (w90)  v19 mid tom (w91)  v20 lo tom (w92) = Simmons toms
#    v21 bottle crack (w87) + v22 glass shatter (w5)
#    v38 sub boom sine (w0) + v40 slowed kick thud (w82 f110)
#    v26 synth pad root (w15) + v27 3rd (w15 left), v28 5th (w16 right)
#
#  DELAY BUSES:
#    Bus 1: Annie vocal lead space echo (DS 1 125 .75, dotted eighth)
#    Bus 2: Main bass riff 16th slapback (DS 2 125 .25)
#    Bus 3: Bottle crack & sub boom reverb tail (DS 3 125 .75)
#    Bus 4: Synth pad & riser stereo wash (DS 4 125 1, DP 4 1)
#
#  ARRANGEMENT (96 bars):
#    0-3   Intro: Lone bass riff + milk bottle crack & sub drop
#    4-7   16th hats enter, filter opens, counter-riff in left channel
#    8-15  Groove drops: 4-on-floor kick, claps, snare, synth pad swells
#    16-23 Verse 1: Annie Lennox vocal ('Some of them want to use you...')
#    24-39 Chorus 1: 'Sweet dreams are made of this...', full energy wall of sound
#    40-47 Bridge: 'Hold your head up, movin' on...' with swelling gospel chords
#    48-55 Analog Synth Solo: screaming pitch bends and portamento slides
#    56-63 Breakdown: Drums cut, delay freezes (DF 1 1), K-synth riser build
#    64-79 Chorus 2 & Climax: Maximum power, high vocal ad-libs, bottle cracks
#    80-87 Verse 2 / Bridge reprise
#    88-95 Outro: Riff vamp, stereo counter-riff, hats half-time, final delay freeze
#    96    End cleanup
# ======================================================================

[SWEET DREAMS - EURYTHMICS] puts
M 125 16

## INLINE K-SYNTH RISER (one-shot wave 301)
[
N: 65536
T: !N
E: (e(T*(4.2%N)))%100
R: r T
L: 0.35 f R
H: R-L
F: 800*(e(T*(2.6%N)))*((p 2)%(p 0))
P: +\F
S: s P
W: w E*((S*.35)+(H*.55))
] k!
k>w301,44100,1

## DELAY BUSES
# Bus 1: Annie Lennox vocal lead & solo space echo (dotted eighth)
DS 1 125 .75
DL 1 - - 8 2 3 11
DD 1 7 2
DP 1 1

# Bus 2: Main bass riff 16th slapback (adds thickness & punch)
DS 2 125 .25
DL 2 - - 4 0 0 8
DD 2 7 3

# Bus 3: Bottle crack & sub boom reverb tail
DS 3 125 .75
DL 3 - - 8 0 0 10
DD 3 5 4

# Bus 4: Synth pad & riser stereo hall wash
DS 4 125 1
DL 4 - - 10 3 6 11
DD 4 8 2
DP 4 1

## VOICES
# Drums: punchy four-on-the-floor kick + sub punch
v0 w82 f440 a7 p0 [kick electronic] vt
v5 w0 a-2 p0 t.001,.22,0,.06 j1 k160 q.7 [kick sub punch] vt

# Crisp 80s gated snare, claps, hats, crash
v1 w83 f440 a8 p0 r3 ds.20 [snare 80s gated] vt
v2 w84 f440 a-3 p.25 [closed hat] vt
v3 w85 f440 a-2 p-.25 [open hat] vt
v4 w86 f440 a7 p0 [electronic clap] vt
v17 w94 f440 a4 p.2 [crash cymbal] vt

# Simmons Electronic Toms (hi, mid, lo)
v18 w90 f480 a6 p-.3 [hi simmons tom] vt
v19 w91 f380 a6 p0 [mid simmons tom] vt
v20 w92 f280 a6 p.3 [lo simmons tom] vt

# The Iconic Sweet Dreams Bass Riff: Roland SH-101 / Juno saw + square
# Sends ds.10 to Bus 2 for subtle slapback width
v6 w15 a-1 p0 t.001,.16,0,.04 j1,2 k1100 q3.2 g0 r2 ds.10 [sweet dreams bass saw] vt
v6 >7
v7 w16 a-5 N0,9 p.45 r0 [sweet dreams bass square] vt
v6 G7 H7

# Left-Panned Counter-Riff (octave up, plucky square with phase distortion c4)
v13 w16 a-7 p-.55 t.002,.15,0,.04 j1,2 k2400 q1.8 c4,.2 r1 ds.25 [counter riff left] vt

# Annie Lennox Vocal Lead: rich, soulful, expressive singing synth with portamento glide
# Soft 50ms attack and long 1.6s decay with safe s=0 prevents any stuck notes
v8 w15 a-5 p0 t.05,1.5,0,.35 j1 k2500 q1.2 g.08 c4,.20 r1 ds.35 [annie vocal lead] vt
v8 >9
v8 >10
v9 w15 a-7 N0,9 p-.5 r0 [annie vocal left] vt
v10 w16 a-8 N0,-9 p.5 r0 [annie vocal right] vt
v8 G9,10 H9,10

# Analog Pitch-Bend Synth Solo: resonant singing saw with 70ms portamento glide
v11 w15 a-5 p0 t.003,.35,0,.10 j1,2 k3400 q3.2 g.07 c4,.25 r1 ds.35 [analog synth solo] vt
v11 >12
v12 w16 a-8 N0,12 p.45 r0 [solo partner] vt
v11 G12 H12

# Dave Stewart's Famous Milk Bottle Crack & Sub Boom Impact
v21 w87 f520 a8 p-.2 [bottle crack] vt
v22 w5 f1800 a-4 p.2 j2 k1800 q2 t.001,.08,0,.03 [bottle glass shatter] vt
v38 w0 a2 p0 t.002,.80,0,.30 j1 k220 q.7 r3 ds.3 [sub boom drop] vt
v40 w82 f110 a5 p0 [sub thud layer] vt

# Riser: stretched K-synth one-shot
v16 w301 f187 a8 p0 t.005,.01,1,.4 r4 ds.3 [ksynth riser] vt

# Warm Analog Synth Pad Chords (Cm -> Ab -> G, delay Bus 4)
v26 w15 a-8 p0 t.08,.60,.3,.35 j1 k2000 q1.0 c4,.15 r4 ds.3 [synth pad root] vt
v27 w15 a-9 N0,8 p-.5 r0 [synth pad 3rd] vt
v28 w16 a-9 N0,-8 p.5 r0 [synth pad 5th] vt
v26 G27,28 H27,28

## EVENTS
[O DQ] /ceb 4 99
/cer 1

## STREAMS (Note arrays converted via n>d)
# Stream 1: The Iconic 2-Bar Sweet Dreams Bass Riff (16 eighth notes / 32 sixteenth steps)
# Bar 1 (Cm): C2 C2 C2 C2  Eb2 Eb2 C2 C2
# Bar 2 (Ab/G): Ab1 Ab1 Ab1 C2  G1 G1 G1 C2
[C2 C2 C2 C2  Eb2 Eb2 C2 C2  Ab1 Ab1 Ab1 C2  G1 G1 G1 C2] n>d /SS 1

# Stream 2: Left-Panned Counter-Riff (12 notes / 32 steps)
[C3 C3 C3 C3  Eb3 Eb3 C3 C3  Ab2 Ab2 Ab2 C3  G2 G2 G2 C3] n>d /SS 2

